00:00:03.431 --> 00:00:05.382
- I just put business in perspective.

00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:06.478
- Put things in perspective.

00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:08.628
- Keep things in perspective.

00:00:08.628 --> 00:00:10.255
- Keep things in perspective.

00:00:10.255 --> 00:00:11.269
- Keep perspective.

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:13.136
- Have a different perspective.

00:00:13.136 --> 00:00:14.431
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:15.814
Today, we're going to talk about

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:18.086
how you can keep things in perspective.

00:00:18.086 --> 00:00:19.912
And as always, guys as you're watching,

00:00:19.912 --> 00:00:21.862
if you hear something
that really inspires you,

00:00:21.862 --> 00:00:23.567
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:24.824
Put quotes around it as well

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.408
so that other people can be inspired.

00:00:26.408 --> 00:00:28.847
When you write it down, it's
much more likely to sink in

00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:30.192
for yourself as well.

00:00:30.192 --> 00:00:31.168
Enjoy.

00:00:31.168 --> 00:00:34.001
(uplifting music)

00:00:42.654 --> 00:00:44.508
- When you have a down time,

00:00:44.508 --> 00:00:46.777
like something didn't
work the way you want,

00:00:46.777 --> 00:00:49.861
what do you do to get
back on that positiveness?

00:00:49.861 --> 00:00:51.695
- I talk to the mountain.

00:00:51.695 --> 00:00:53.605
I have a mountain next to my home

00:00:53.605 --> 00:00:55.147
that is called Rochers de Naye.

00:00:55.147 --> 00:00:57.257
It goes up to two, it's very low.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:01:00.090
It goes up to 2400 or 2500 meters.

00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:03.511
Or I talk to the Dents de Midi,

00:01:03.511 --> 00:01:05.903
which is 4000 meters which is a little bit

00:01:05.903 --> 00:01:07.447
further away from my home.

00:01:07.447 --> 00:01:09.640
Which I see every morning.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.870
I see those two mountains.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.577
And I say to these two mountains,

00:01:13.577 --> 00:01:17.771
Mountains, I have a problem,
but when I look at you,

00:01:17.771 --> 00:01:20.193
you are 37 billion old.

00:01:20.193 --> 00:01:21.977
(laughs)

00:01:21.977 --> 00:01:26.522
And I'm a little guy here
with a little problem.

00:01:26.522 --> 00:01:28.228
Can you help me?

00:01:28.228 --> 00:01:30.867
They will say come on.

00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:35.630
Look what we have already
seen in so many years.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.213
Your problem is a nano-problem.

00:01:39.655 --> 00:01:40.672
Come on, get up.

00:01:40.672 --> 00:01:42.437
- Just get up, do it.

00:01:42.437 --> 00:01:43.753
- That's it.

00:01:43.753 --> 00:01:47.164
- My question is, I'm an
entrepreneur, it's very great,

00:01:47.164 --> 00:01:49.684
but not all days are great in a company.

00:01:49.684 --> 00:01:53.180
So what are your tips and
tricks for tough days?

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.318
- I think there's massive
confusion around entrepreneurship.

00:01:56.318 --> 00:01:57.790
Entrepreneurship sucks.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.228
I mean it's lonely, it's high risk.

00:02:00.228 --> 00:02:02.097
I mean I can't live without it.

00:02:02.097 --> 00:02:04.615
But it's like a bad boyfriend
or girlfriend, right.

00:02:04.615 --> 00:02:07.987
There's a ton of bad days
being an entrepreneur.

00:02:07.987 --> 00:02:10.306
Not to mention 98% of
entrepreneurial ventures

00:02:10.306 --> 00:02:11.322
are going to fail.

00:02:11.322 --> 00:02:13.069
So there's going to be a
really bad (bleeped) day

00:02:13.069 --> 00:02:13.922
in your future.

00:02:13.922 --> 00:02:15.827
(crowd laughs)

00:02:15.827 --> 00:02:18.330
Um, you know, hopefully not for you.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.580
Um, or any of you.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.717
And you know, for me,

00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:23.785
I think this is a very personal question.

00:02:23.785 --> 00:02:25.695
I think it's how you're wired.

00:02:25.695 --> 00:02:28.927
I'm so all-in entrepreneur
I prefer the pain.

00:02:28.927 --> 00:02:30.919
I think one of the reasons
I love the Jets so much

00:02:30.919 --> 00:02:32.828
is because they bring me so much pain.

00:02:32.828 --> 00:02:35.078
You know, I love the climb.

00:02:36.527 --> 00:02:39.737
To me, the set back is exciting.

00:02:39.737 --> 00:02:41.772
I love when something goes wrong.

00:02:41.772 --> 00:02:43.637
It's where I shine the most.

00:02:43.637 --> 00:02:46.075
But that's not for everybody, right.

00:02:46.075 --> 00:02:47.417
It can be very difficult.

00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:49.120
And when you start affecting your life

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.191
and your loved ones and all other things,

00:02:51.191 --> 00:02:52.938
it can get real nasty.

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:56.667
To me, the way I handle things
even on the few rare days

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.494
when I really struggle,

00:02:58.494 --> 00:03:00.935
I take a real step back and make pretend

00:03:00.935 --> 00:03:02.519
that somebody called me and told me

00:03:02.519 --> 00:03:05.280
that my mother or daughter were killed.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.322
And I know that's very
dark and I apologize,

00:03:08.322 --> 00:03:09.872
but it's really what I do.

00:03:09.872 --> 00:03:12.924
I literally am able to at my
deepest, most struggling moment

00:03:12.924 --> 00:03:16.052
within business take a step back

00:03:16.052 --> 00:03:19.632
and remind myself that I
could make a drillion dollars

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:23.447
tomorrow on bitcoin and
if something bad happen

00:03:23.447 --> 00:03:25.191
to the people I love the most

00:03:25.191 --> 00:03:26.735
that it would mean nothing.

00:03:26.735 --> 00:03:31.236
And very consistently
rewires me very quickly.

00:03:31.236 --> 00:03:33.795
I just put business in perspective.

00:03:33.795 --> 00:03:37.078
At the end of the day, it's money...

00:03:37.078 --> 00:03:38.866
For me, it's not really
money, it's my legacy.

00:03:38.866 --> 00:03:42.033
So I get hurt by it a little bit more.

00:03:42.899 --> 00:03:46.353
You know, I put it in
perspective, it's money.

00:03:46.353 --> 00:03:48.792
And you know what, up
until I had a daughter,

00:03:48.792 --> 00:03:50.089
even while I was married,

00:03:50.089 --> 00:03:52.974
up until when I had Mischa four years ago,

00:03:52.974 --> 00:03:55.815
I secretly wanted to lose all my money.

00:03:55.815 --> 00:03:59.876
I had this weird, twisted, dark fantasy

00:03:59.876 --> 00:04:02.674
of losing everything just to rise again

00:04:02.674 --> 00:04:05.962
like a Phoenix and remind you (bleeped).

00:04:05.962 --> 00:04:08.360
- Do you feel underrated as a rapper?

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.948
- Not as of lately.

00:04:09.948 --> 00:04:11.288
Like which is crazy.

00:04:11.288 --> 00:04:13.397
For a long time man,
for years, I was pissed.

00:04:13.397 --> 00:04:15.425
So a song on the album called Buried Alive

00:04:15.425 --> 00:04:17.173
is about that exact thing.

00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:19.527
You know, it's about me kind of going

00:04:19.527 --> 00:04:21.353
well how come he gets
the so and so cosigner,

00:04:21.353 --> 00:04:23.344
how come he gets that or
how come they get that.

00:04:23.344 --> 00:04:24.233
I can tour the world.

00:04:24.233 --> 00:04:25.168
I can sell out shows.

00:04:25.168 --> 00:04:26.346
I got fans, I got this.

00:04:26.346 --> 00:04:28.752
What the (bleep) man, like being angry.

00:04:28.752 --> 00:04:30.093
You know, I had a friend tell me,

00:04:30.093 --> 00:04:32.695
she basically said those same people

00:04:32.695 --> 00:04:35.945
who had the cosigns and have
the this and have the looks

00:04:35.945 --> 00:04:37.405
are the same people are going

00:04:37.405 --> 00:04:39.315
how come I ain't got fans like this then

00:04:39.315 --> 00:04:40.898
and how come I can't tour on my own.

00:04:40.898 --> 00:04:42.117
How come I can't this?

00:04:42.117 --> 00:04:43.294
Like what the (bleep).

00:04:43.294 --> 00:04:44.921
So it kind of put things
in perspective for me

00:04:44.921 --> 00:04:46.910
and let me go, okay, I don't have it yet,

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.979
but if I keep fighting
and I keep working hard

00:04:48.979 --> 00:04:50.526
and I keep staying on this path,

00:04:50.526 --> 00:04:51.499
it's going to happen.

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:53.609
You know, and as of late
within the last few months man,

00:04:53.609 --> 00:04:56.620
just from releasing the
singles and the music videos

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.690
and like this solid body of work,

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.664
I've truly began to get what I deserve.

00:05:01.664 --> 00:05:06.372
- 13 years ago, you were
completely bust, gone.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.705
No money, you had five
pounds, you know seven dollars

00:05:09.705 --> 00:05:10.921
left in your hand.

00:05:10.921 --> 00:05:13.759
You used it for a taxi
back to your parents.

00:05:13.759 --> 00:05:15.466
And your career in the record business

00:05:15.466 --> 00:05:18.880
had just come to sudden, shuddering halt.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.343
And here you are 13 years later,

00:05:20.343 --> 00:05:22.293
you're worth hundreds
of millions of dollars,

00:05:22.293 --> 00:05:24.366
life's taken a huge turn up,

00:05:24.366 --> 00:05:26.195
but I get the sense with you

00:05:26.195 --> 00:05:29.487
that what happen to you 13
years ago still defines you now.

00:05:29.487 --> 00:05:31.762
- Yeah, I mean it wasn't
the best of times,

00:05:31.762 --> 00:05:33.266
but then again when I look back on it,

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.651
it wasn't the worst of times.

00:05:34.651 --> 00:05:38.106
You know, because I think
particularly here in Hollywood,

00:05:38.106 --> 00:05:40.504
where most people get it wrong

00:05:40.504 --> 00:05:43.064
is they're afraid of
losing what they've got.

00:05:43.064 --> 00:05:45.293
They're just terrified
of losing their fame,

00:05:45.293 --> 00:05:47.241
as you said, power, money.

00:05:47.241 --> 00:05:50.248
But actually once you've lost it,

00:05:50.248 --> 00:05:51.672
you can always get it back again.

00:05:51.672 --> 00:05:53.092
I mean it's not the end of the world.

00:05:53.092 --> 00:05:54.716
I mean being ill is worse.

00:05:54.716 --> 00:05:56.909
So because I've actually faced

00:05:56.909 --> 00:06:00.557
one of most people's worst
fears and recovered from it,

00:06:00.557 --> 00:06:02.140
it's not as bad as you think.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:04.701
You know, I didn't lose my confidence.

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.694
My friends were still my friends.

00:06:06.694 --> 00:06:08.362
I've lived with my parents.

00:06:08.362 --> 00:06:10.147
And I just saw it as a challenge

00:06:10.147 --> 00:06:12.337
that I've got to get myself
back on my feet again.

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:14.451
- What advice did your
parents give you there?

00:06:14.451 --> 00:06:17.296
- Honest to god, they
were just cool about it.

00:06:17.296 --> 00:06:19.041
You know, they were parents.

00:06:19.041 --> 00:06:20.218
They just, you know,
want to look after me,

00:06:20.218 --> 00:06:21.641
lived with them for a while.

00:06:21.641 --> 00:06:23.872
My dad lent me some money to pay the bank.

00:06:23.872 --> 00:06:26.715
Then, eventually I managed
to pay my Dad back.

00:06:26.715 --> 00:06:29.637
You know, it was what any parent would do.

00:06:29.637 --> 00:06:33.985
But like I said, it wasn't
the worst time of my life.

00:06:33.985 --> 00:06:36.422
Actually, when I look back
on it now, I still smile,

00:06:36.422 --> 00:06:39.884
because I bought this beat
up old British sports car,

00:06:39.884 --> 00:06:43.820
worked 18 hours a day and
I was so determined, Piers,

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.849
just to get it right this time.

00:06:45.849 --> 00:06:48.000
Cause I knew I'd got it wrong.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.804
So now, I find it much
easier to deal with things.

00:06:50.804 --> 00:06:53.489
- If that wasn't the worst
time of your life, what was?

00:06:53.489 --> 00:06:56.088
- Well, when my Dad died was
the worst time of my life.

00:06:56.088 --> 00:06:58.076
As you know, you and I discussed that.

00:06:58.076 --> 00:07:01.853
That you know, like getting
ill, losing a parent,

00:07:01.853 --> 00:07:04.048
or losing somebody close to you,

00:07:04.048 --> 00:07:06.643
that's the worst thing that
could ever happen in your life.

00:07:06.643 --> 00:07:09.240
In all the things that I worry about now,

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.823
it's just trivial.

00:07:10.823 --> 00:07:13.907
I mean even the whole kind
of Idol, X-Factor thing,

00:07:13.907 --> 00:07:18.651
I laugh about it because it's
such a high class problem.

00:07:18.651 --> 00:07:20.279
My show is better than your show.

00:07:20.279 --> 00:07:22.351
It's like we both got a show.

00:07:22.351 --> 00:07:23.609
(laughs)

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:25.033
I mean what's the problem.

00:07:25.033 --> 00:07:26.577
- It's a bit like Colin
Firth and Hugh Grant

00:07:26.577 --> 00:07:28.364
in the fountain in Bridget Jones fighting.

00:07:28.364 --> 00:07:29.703
- Exactly, over what?

00:07:29.703 --> 00:07:31.811
I mean the fact that we're
here and we can do this,

00:07:31.811 --> 00:07:32.867
it's fantastic.

00:07:32.867 --> 00:07:35.034
- Before every one of my debates,

00:07:35.034 --> 00:07:38.653
I did something to keep
things in perspective.

00:07:38.653 --> 00:07:40.764
To keep myself grounded.

00:07:40.764 --> 00:07:42.671
At the top of a sheet of paper

00:07:42.671 --> 00:07:44.461
that was always placed on the podium

00:07:44.461 --> 00:07:46.655
so we could make notes during the debate,

00:07:46.655 --> 00:07:48.846
just before the debate kicked off,

00:07:48.846 --> 00:07:51.596
I wrote at the top one word, dad.

00:07:52.986 --> 00:07:56.118
I also drew a small image of the Sun.

00:07:56.118 --> 00:07:58.920
And throughout the debate
when I glanced down

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.832
at that paper to look at
my notes that I had taken,

00:08:00.832 --> 00:08:03.227
I was reminded of my father's fearlessness

00:08:03.227 --> 00:08:06.389
in fighting for what
he believed was right.

00:08:06.389 --> 00:08:08.259
And the Sun that reminded me

00:08:08.259 --> 00:08:10.450
of course of that familiar scripture,

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.241
let your light so shine.

00:08:12.241 --> 00:08:13.862
Win or lose that debate,

00:08:13.862 --> 00:08:16.538
I hoped that I would never do anything

00:08:16.538 --> 00:08:18.160
that would dishonor or discredit

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.438
the things I hold most dear.

00:08:20.438 --> 00:08:22.676
Now during your life,

00:08:22.676 --> 00:08:25.077
you're going to encounter circumstances

00:08:25.077 --> 00:08:27.229
that make you sweat.

00:08:27.229 --> 00:08:29.666
For many of you, the exams
and tests won't be over

00:08:29.666 --> 00:08:31.451
when you graduate.

00:08:31.451 --> 00:08:33.800
And you're all going to stand at podiums,

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.361
stand in front of a boss to ask for raise,

00:08:36.361 --> 00:08:38.307
or work on some critical project

00:08:38.307 --> 00:08:40.423
in your employment that
will make a big difference

00:08:40.423 --> 00:08:42.055
in your life.

00:08:42.055 --> 00:08:43.799
At moments like those,

00:08:43.799 --> 00:08:46.966
perspective is a very powerful friend.

00:08:49.201 --> 00:08:53.061
You can welcome perspective
through preparatory prayer

00:08:53.061 --> 00:08:55.620
by considering the blessings of the temple

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.508
or by simply glancing at your CTR ring.

00:08:58.508 --> 00:09:02.609
Find ways to keep your
life in perspective.

00:09:02.609 --> 00:09:04.773
- When I was 20, I worked for this,

00:09:04.773 --> 00:09:06.560
I grew up in Malvern in New York,

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.509
I worked for the sanitation department.

00:09:08.509 --> 00:09:09.687
I was a garbage man.

00:09:09.687 --> 00:09:10.986
- You were a garbage man?

00:09:10.986 --> 00:09:12.044
- I was a garbage man.

00:09:12.044 --> 00:09:14.766
I worked the back of the
truck, 22 square blocks.

00:09:14.766 --> 00:09:15.766
That's hard.

00:09:16.955 --> 00:09:19.190
Doing movies is, there's
nothing that we do

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:20.775
in the movies that's hard.

00:09:20.775 --> 00:09:23.739
- I used to deliver for United
Parcel Service on a truck.

00:09:23.739 --> 00:09:25.042
That was hard.

00:09:25.042 --> 00:09:25.875
- Yeah.

00:09:25.875 --> 00:09:26.829
- This is a joke.

00:09:26.829 --> 00:09:28.854
- People always say why do you spend

00:09:28.854 --> 00:09:30.636
so much time preparing and everything,

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:32.181
cause there's a bunch
of other guys out there

00:09:32.181 --> 00:09:33.348
that would want my job

00:09:33.348 --> 00:09:34.593
and I'm not going to do
anything to mess it up.

00:09:34.593 --> 00:09:35.648
- That's right.

00:09:35.648 --> 00:09:36.926
- Keep things in perspective.

00:09:36.926 --> 00:09:37.778
I know we all say it,

00:09:37.778 --> 00:09:40.257
but really you have to
keep reinforcing it.

00:09:40.257 --> 00:09:42.853
You know all of, everyone
in this audience,

00:09:42.853 --> 00:09:45.569
you know knock on wood,
you're going to do just fine.

00:09:45.569 --> 00:09:47.964
You're going to have
your four bedroom house.

00:09:47.964 --> 00:09:51.176
You're going to have your
car with power windows.

00:09:51.176 --> 00:09:54.796
You'll be able to go to
Seaworld whenever you want to.

00:09:54.796 --> 00:09:58.941
But along that way, there are
going to be ups and downs.

00:09:58.941 --> 00:10:01.989
And actually those ups and
downs then to happen a lot

00:10:01.989 --> 00:10:04.064
when you go to transition points.

00:10:04.064 --> 00:10:05.523
When you're entering the work force,

00:10:05.523 --> 00:10:08.244
you're entering some type
of new phase in your life.

00:10:08.244 --> 00:10:11.858
And you just always have to keep on

00:10:11.858 --> 00:10:13.363
kind of the long term game, the end game.

00:10:13.363 --> 00:10:15.518
And you know, I'll tell you myself,

00:10:15.518 --> 00:10:18.159
I've gone through fairly dramatic ones

00:10:18.159 --> 00:10:19.946
right when I was out of the gate.

00:10:19.946 --> 00:10:22.428
You know when I was, this was 1998,

00:10:22.428 --> 00:10:24.254
I had just graduated.

00:10:24.254 --> 00:10:26.894
I was a few months older
than most of you all.

00:10:26.894 --> 00:10:30.713
And some computer magazine
had seen something I had done

00:10:30.713 --> 00:10:33.267
and they wrote this neat profile about me.

00:10:33.267 --> 00:10:35.419
They called it Future So Bright

00:10:35.419 --> 00:10:37.897
and I saw that magazine,
I was very proud of it.

00:10:37.897 --> 00:10:38.995
I was like, oh look, I'm set.

00:10:38.995 --> 00:10:40.986
I have this career ahead of me.

00:10:40.986 --> 00:10:43.099
I'm already profiled in a magazine.

00:10:43.099 --> 00:10:46.349
And frankly, I got kind of into myself.

00:10:47.363 --> 00:10:49.514
And it's okay, you can
enjoy your successes,

00:10:49.514 --> 00:10:52.030
but I didn't have any perspective.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:55.567
And frankly, it was a
dangerous thing to have happen.

00:10:55.567 --> 00:10:57.725
And to really put things in perspective,

00:10:57.725 --> 00:10:59.716
and I'm happy it did happen,

00:10:59.716 --> 00:11:02.340
two months later I had
kind of switched jobs

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:03.763
and you know higher salary.

00:11:03.763 --> 00:11:06.281
I thought I was on the fast track.

00:11:06.281 --> 00:11:10.382
And I had a new boss and on
the first three days of work,

00:11:10.382 --> 00:11:12.985
he spent an hour just
completely castigating me.

00:11:12.985 --> 00:11:16.238
Essentially telling me that
I was not worth his time.

00:11:16.238 --> 00:11:19.968
That I was incompetent as
far as he was concerned.

00:11:19.968 --> 00:11:22.605
And so you can imagine, like a lot of you,

00:11:22.605 --> 00:11:23.825
successful my whole life,

00:11:23.825 --> 00:11:26.426
fancy degrees from fancy universities,

00:11:26.426 --> 00:11:28.823
two months ago I was
profiled in a magazine

00:11:28.823 --> 00:11:33.815
and then now, all of sudden,
not even 23 years old,

00:11:33.815 --> 00:11:37.516
I was back in a hotel room in
the middle of nowhere crying.

00:11:37.516 --> 00:11:39.634
Not knowing what I was
going to do with my life.

00:11:39.634 --> 00:11:41.830
Convinced that it was all
the end of everything,

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.170
everything was for not.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:44.739
And you know, so you get through them,

00:11:44.739 --> 00:11:46.059
you wake up in the morning,

00:11:46.059 --> 00:11:47.526
things look a little bit better.

00:11:47.526 --> 00:11:49.189
A week later, things look a little better.

00:11:49.189 --> 00:11:50.732
You start circulating your resume around.

00:11:50.732 --> 00:11:53.070
I did find another job two months later.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:54.237
And it's okay.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:57.490
And the one thing I want to stress,

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.442
because I've gone through ups and downs

00:11:59.442 --> 00:12:01.808
and you only have one
perspective for your own life,

00:12:01.808 --> 00:12:03.020
but I suspect many of you all

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:04.634
are going to have higher ups than I've had

00:12:04.634 --> 00:12:07.684
and many of you all are
going to have lower downs.

00:12:07.684 --> 00:12:10.517
And I worry about that some times.

00:12:11.464 --> 00:12:13.696
The ones of you that have higher ups,

00:12:13.696 --> 00:12:15.363
just keep them in perspective.

00:12:15.363 --> 00:12:16.196
And it's inevitable.

00:12:16.196 --> 00:12:17.964
Some of you are going to race ahead

00:12:17.964 --> 00:12:21.253
and be so successful that no
of us can imagine it right now.

00:12:21.253 --> 00:12:22.511
But keep them in perspective.

00:12:22.511 --> 00:12:24.783
Enjoy the successes,

00:12:24.783 --> 00:12:27.789
but when your ego starts
a little bit large,

00:12:27.789 --> 00:12:30.673
keep in mind the Sun
will supernova one day,

00:12:30.673 --> 00:12:32.703
the galaxies will collide.

00:12:32.703 --> 00:12:35.549
We are these small little
mammals on this small planet.

00:12:35.549 --> 00:12:38.633
Or you know, there's 100, 200
billion stars in the galaxy,

00:12:38.633 --> 00:12:40.381
in just our galaxy alone.

00:12:40.381 --> 00:12:44.279
And just have peace in the little success.

00:12:44.279 --> 00:12:46.637
And when you have a hard time,

00:12:46.637 --> 00:12:49.315
and you will and some will
go through painful periods,

00:12:49.315 --> 00:12:50.860
you might stumble and start

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:52.648
your first few times out the gate.

00:12:52.648 --> 00:12:55.653
Also keep in perspective
that those stresses,

00:12:55.653 --> 00:12:57.560
put them in perspective of the universe.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:58.495
They are small.

00:12:58.495 --> 00:12:59.712
They are going to be things

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:01.618
that you'll be able to
laugh about, talk about,

00:13:01.618 --> 00:13:04.700
attend 15 years from now or
hopefully 10-15 days from then.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.289
- Keep perspective.

00:13:06.289 --> 00:13:08.158
And that's the hardest
thing to tell somebody

00:13:08.158 --> 00:13:09.862
when they are going through a hard time,

00:13:09.862 --> 00:13:11.405
because you know it's so easy to say

00:13:11.405 --> 00:13:14.206
well you don't understand
me or this is so hard

00:13:14.206 --> 00:13:16.315
or this is the worst time in my life.

00:13:16.315 --> 00:13:18.876
And some of that might feel true.

00:13:18.876 --> 00:13:19.893
And it might be true.

00:13:19.893 --> 00:13:22.450
It might be one of the most
difficult, trying times

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:23.533
of your life.

00:13:24.521 --> 00:13:26.548
And all we can say is keep perspective.

00:13:26.548 --> 00:13:28.052
We can't say keep perspective,

00:13:28.052 --> 00:13:31.380
other than just say there
have been good times.

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:32.718
Remember them.

00:13:32.718 --> 00:13:35.960
Don't cut loose of those
good times in your memories,

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.966
just because now your
focus is on the dark times.

00:13:38.966 --> 00:13:41.841
Remember those times that were better.

00:13:41.841 --> 00:13:45.047
Remember those times in which
you did connect with others,

00:13:45.047 --> 00:13:49.022
that you did create,
that you did take action.

00:13:49.022 --> 00:13:50.809
And remember also your strength,

00:13:50.809 --> 00:13:53.077
because it's so easy when times are dark

00:13:53.077 --> 00:13:54.938
to just focus on all the things

00:13:54.938 --> 00:13:56.466
that you're doing to screw it up.

00:13:56.466 --> 00:13:58.015
Or all the things that people are doing

00:13:58.015 --> 00:13:59.070
to mess with your life,

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:01.548
and you forget the incredible
power that you have.

00:14:01.548 --> 00:14:04.593
I mean it is an amazing miracle,

00:14:04.593 --> 00:14:06.099
if you're looking for the miracle,

00:14:06.099 --> 00:14:07.521
you already got it.

00:14:07.521 --> 00:14:09.678
That miracle that you've
been given the power of,

00:14:09.678 --> 00:14:13.845
choice and will to direct
your own attention each day,

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:17.563
to direct your own attitude each day,

00:14:17.563 --> 00:14:20.003
to direct your own actions each day,

00:14:20.003 --> 00:14:22.030
to direct your own affections

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:23.900
and emotions out into the world.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:25.402
That you control those things.

00:14:25.402 --> 00:14:27.031
That you can move those things.

00:14:27.031 --> 00:14:28.658
That you can shape those things.

00:14:28.658 --> 00:14:29.795
That's the miracle.

00:14:29.795 --> 00:14:31.462
You are the miracle.

00:14:32.433 --> 00:14:34.994
You've been waiting for
something to show up and change

00:14:34.994 --> 00:14:37.436
and I just say you've
already been given the gift.

00:14:37.436 --> 00:14:40.627
Now, you have to activate it.

00:14:40.627 --> 00:14:41.885
So when it's difficult,

00:14:41.885 --> 00:14:43.200
keep perspective on the fact

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.365
that there have been good times,

00:14:44.365 --> 00:14:45.729
there will be more good times,

00:14:45.729 --> 00:14:47.711
even if you are struggling personally,

00:14:47.711 --> 00:14:50.106
you still have that great freedom

00:14:50.106 --> 00:14:51.534
that has been given to us,

00:14:51.534 --> 00:14:53.747
and that choice and gift of free will

00:14:53.747 --> 00:14:55.696
to start directing yourself.

00:14:55.696 --> 00:14:58.111
- I mean obviously you can't
come on a show like this

00:14:58.111 --> 00:15:01.368
without the mention of the
wanking in the toilet thing.

00:15:01.368 --> 00:15:02.908
(crowd laughs)

00:15:02.908 --> 00:15:04.936
- Which wanking in the
toilet thing? Which one?

00:15:04.936 --> 00:15:05.769
- The arrest.

00:15:05.769 --> 00:15:06.939
- Oh, of course. That one.

00:15:06.939 --> 00:15:08.746
- Yeah, the one we've heard about.

00:15:08.746 --> 00:15:11.586
(crowd laughs)

00:15:11.586 --> 00:15:13.168
- The time I got caught you mean.

00:15:13.168 --> 00:15:15.918
(crowd applause)

00:15:20.604 --> 00:15:21.861
- See, this is the thing.

00:15:21.861 --> 00:15:23.773
The way you talk about it is

00:15:23.773 --> 00:15:26.775
your fantastic, sort of
unapologetic about it.

00:15:26.775 --> 00:15:28.398
And you didn't go into hiding.

00:15:28.398 --> 00:15:31.765
You didn't sort of, you
know draw the curtains.

00:15:31.765 --> 00:15:34.728
Was it the next night, you
were out in a restaurant

00:15:34.728 --> 00:15:35.824
in LA having dinner.

00:15:35.824 --> 00:15:36.657
- Absolutely.

00:15:36.657 --> 00:15:38.178
Well, I mean what's to apologize for.

00:15:38.178 --> 00:15:39.357
You know, I'm a gay man.

00:15:39.357 --> 00:15:41.913
At the time, I was like 36 years old.

00:15:41.913 --> 00:15:43.310
If I'm perfectly honest,

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:45.267
if I'm perfectly, perfectly honest,

00:15:45.267 --> 00:15:48.557
outside of my career, I've
had a terrible run of luck

00:15:48.557 --> 00:15:50.706
that started about 10 years ago.

00:15:50.706 --> 00:15:53.549
I've watched a partner die.

00:15:53.549 --> 00:15:55.174
I've watched my mother die.

00:15:55.174 --> 00:15:58.924
Just after that, I went
to see a back surgeon

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:03.870
who told me if I didn't
have two vertebrae removed

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:05.821
within the next six months to a year

00:16:05.821 --> 00:16:06.919
that I could be paralyzed.

00:16:06.919 --> 00:16:09.107
So you just learn to have
a different perspective.

00:16:09.107 --> 00:16:11.865
I don't give a toss if people
have real problem with me,

00:16:11.865 --> 00:16:12.837
you know...

00:16:12.837 --> 00:16:15.587
(crowd applause)

00:16:19.727 --> 00:16:21.235
I have a different perspective on life.

00:16:21.235 --> 00:16:22.290
I lost a lot of great things,

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:24.685
but I still have a lot
of incredible things.

00:16:24.685 --> 00:16:26.759
And the press doesn't
really enter into it.

00:16:26.759 --> 00:16:29.773
- I want my daughter to grow up thinking

00:16:29.773 --> 00:16:32.211
that the phrase working woman sounds

00:16:32.211 --> 00:16:35.134
as odd and superficial and forced

00:16:35.134 --> 00:16:36.923
as the phrase working man.

00:16:36.923 --> 00:16:41.269
My husband is my greatest
source of motivation.

00:16:41.269 --> 00:16:43.784
- She always has it in her to accomplish

00:16:43.784 --> 00:16:45.285
whatever she puts her mind to.

00:16:45.285 --> 00:16:47.361
- He's the person I lean on the most.

00:16:47.361 --> 00:16:49.394
- I always tell Ivanka don't worry

00:16:49.394 --> 00:16:51.180
about the things you can't control.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:53.212
Just worry about how you react to

00:16:53.212 --> 00:16:57.108
and deal with the circumstances
and situations at hand.

00:16:57.108 --> 00:17:00.151
- In the moments of
highest anxiety for me,

00:17:00.151 --> 00:17:03.234
I will think about Jared and the kids

00:17:04.292 --> 00:17:08.292
and realize that no matter
how poorly I perform,

00:17:09.866 --> 00:17:11.736
I will come home that night

00:17:11.736 --> 00:17:14.903
and my kids will not love me any less.

00:17:16.126 --> 00:17:19.094
And my husband will love me just as much.

00:17:19.094 --> 00:17:20.803
Maybe even a little bit more,

00:17:20.803 --> 00:17:22.707
because he'll know I need it.

00:17:22.707 --> 00:17:24.048
- I'm still waiting to see the time

00:17:24.048 --> 00:17:25.750
that she doesn't perform very well.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.379
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:17:27.379 --> 00:17:29.410
I love to know what did
you think of this video.

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:32.210
What lesson did you learn that
you love the most about this?

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.930
How do you keep things in
perspective for yourself?

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:36.795
Leave it down in the comments below

00:17:36.795 --> 00:17:38.419
and I'm join in the discussion.

00:17:38.419 --> 00:17:41.230
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Takosha Swan.

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:42.693
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:17:42.693 --> 00:17:43.547
Your One Word.

00:17:43.547 --> 00:17:45.583
It really, really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:17:45.583 --> 00:17:47.356
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:17:47.356 --> 00:17:48.414
I believe in you.

00:17:48.414 --> 00:17:50.320
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.193
And whatever your one word is.

00:17:52.193 --> 00:17:53.573
Much love.

00:17:53.573 --> 00:17:55.073
I'll see you soon.

